-﻿# macOS
+# macOS
 
-macOS releases of SubScraper are not available at this time, however you can run SubScraper on macOS using Docker.
-Please refer to the [Docker](/installation/docker) page for instructions on how to run SubScraper in a Docker container.
-If you do not have Docker installed, you can download it from [here](https://docs.docker.com/desktop/install/mac-install/).
+## Requirements
+
+- macOS 13 (Ventura) or later, on Apple Silicon or Intel.
+- An internet connection the first time SubScraper needs to install FFmpeg and FFprobe.
+
+## Installation
+
+1. Navigate to the SubScraper [releases page](https://git.subnabbit.com/subscraper/SubScraper/releases), and download the latest
+   `SubScraperVx.x.x-osx-arm64.tar.gz` release. Use this package on both Apple Silicon and Intel Macs; on Intel Macs the
+   app runs under Rosetta 2.
+2. Extract the archive. Your folder should contain `SubScraper.app`, `.playwright`, and `cdm` folders as well as the
+   main files below:
+    - SubScraper.app
+    - SubScraper - Classic
+    - config.conf
+    - rules.json
+3. Before the first run, open `config.conf` and configure the required `Site.BaseUrl` and `Site.DrmCdnHost` values. See the
+   [configuration reference](/config/configuration) for details. The application stops at startup while either value is blank.
+4. Once you have done this, open SubScraper.app (or run `SubScraper - Classic` from Terminal for the classic,
+   text-based version of SubScraper).
+
+!!! warning "Unidentified developer"
+
+    Until SubScraper ships signed releases, macOS Gatekeeper blocks the app with *"SubScraper can't be opened because
+    the developer cannot be verified"*. To open it anyway, right-click (or Control-click) `SubScraper.app`, choose
+    **Open**, then choose **Open** again in the dialog. macOS remembers your choice afterwards. Alternatively, run
+    `xattr -cr /path/to/SubScraper.app` in Terminal to clear the quarantine flag.
+
+## FFmpeg installation
+
+When FFmpeg Path and FFprobe Path are blank, missing, or invalid, SubScraper offers to install FFmpeg automatically.
+On macOS it downloads the current macOS build from
+[ffbinaries](https://github.com/ffbinaries/ffbinaries-prebuilt/releases) (version 6.1, Intel 64-bit) and caches it under
+`~/Library/Application Support/SubScraper/ffmpeg/macos-x64`, reusing it on later runs.
+
+!!! note "Apple Silicon"
+
+    The macOS FFmpeg build is Intel-only: on Apple Silicon Macs it runs through Rosetta 2. If Rosetta is not installed,
+    macOS offers to install it the first time the tools run; you can also install it yourself beforehand with
+    `softwareupdate --install-rosetta --agree-to-license`.
+
+If you prefer, install FFmpeg yourself with [Homebrew](https://brew.sh) (`brew install ffmpeg`) and leave the paths
+blank: SubScraper detects the Homebrew installation automatically. You can also set FFmpeg Path and FFprobe Path
+manually in `config.conf`.
+
+## Docker
+
+You can also run SubScraper on macOS using Docker. Please refer to the [Docker](/installation/docker) page for
+instructions on how to run SubScraper in a Docker container. If you do not have Docker installed, you can download it
+from [here](https://docs.docker.com/desktop/install/mac-install/).
 
 The official Docker image supports both Intel Macs (`linux/amd64`) and Apple Silicon Macs (`linux/arm64`). Docker
 Desktop selects the correct image automatically; no `--platform` option or Rosetta emulation is required.
+
+## Building from source
+
+- Install the [.NET 10 SDK](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dotnet/core/install/macos) and
+  [Homebrew FFmpeg](https://brew.sh) (`brew install ffmpeg`).
+- Clone the repo
+
+```bash
+git clone https://git.subnabbit.com/subscraper/SubScraper.git
+cd 'SubScraper'
+```
+
+- Publish the app. Replace `%VERSION%` with the current version number of SubScraper (e.g. `1.9.20`).
+
+    - Modern graphical version (recommended)
+    ```bash
+    dotnet publish "SubScraper.Gui/SubScraper.Gui.csproj" -p:Version=%VERSION% -p:PackageVersion=%VERSION% -c Release -r osx-arm64 --self-contained
+    ```
+
+    - Classic text-based version
+    ```bash
+    dotnet publish "SubScraper.Cli/SubScraper.Cli.csproj" -p:Version=%VERSION% -p:PackageVersion=%VERSION% -c Release -r osx-arm64 --self-contained
+    ```
+
+- (Optional) Assemble the `.app` bundle:
+
+```bash
+bash scripts/package-macos.sh outosx-arm64-gui %VERSION% .
+```
+
+- Run `SubScraper.app` (or the CLI binary from the publish output directory).
